# Goal 11: Fix modf — NaN handling

## Function
`modf` (double)

## Source Files
- C source: `/home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/libm/mathd/modfd.c`
- Rust source: `/home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/newexp/rust-s3/src/mathd.rs` (~line 3422)

## Problem
Wrong fractional part for NaN input. `modf(nan)` should return `(nan, nan)` (fractional=nan, integer=nan), but Rust returns `(0x0p+0, nan)` — the integer part is correct but the fractional part is 0 instead of NaN.

## What Needs to Change
Read the C source for modf's NaN handling. The Rust implementation likely doesn't have an early return for NaN, or it computes the fractional part incorrectly when the input is NaN. Add/fix the NaN check to return (NaN, NaN) when the input is NaN.

## Success Criteria
- `modf(nan)` returns `(nan, nan)` where fractional=nan and integer=nan — bitwise match with C
- All other modf test cases continue to pass
